n of the estrogen receptor α (ESR1). Since LIX1 is regulated by RAD21, and RAD21 is activated by ESR1, the inhibition of ESR1 by NR3C1 leads to reduced activation of RAD21. Consequently, the expression of LIX1 remains unchanged because the downstream activation of LIX1 by RAD21 is suppressed without being significantly stimulated.", "reasoning_id": 0, "triplets_ref": [["Dex", "targets", "NR3C1"], ["NR3C1", "inhibits", "ESR1"], ["ESR1", "activates", "RAD21"], ["RAD21", "regulates", "LIX1"]], "path_length": 4}}
